          <Pad Id="V712STHWGeGOE7HNa08xYR" Bounds="2203,509,867,311" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="The NotificationsService is the central hub for handling all user input in your application. It captures raw interactions like mouse movements, clicks, keyboard presses, and touch events and organizes them into clean, easy-to-use data streams.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;This service provides:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Focus &amp; Enabled State: Streams that tell you if your application window is currently active and accepting input.&#xD;&#xA;Mouse: A stream with the mouse's current position, button states (left, right, middle), and wheel movement.&#xD;&#xA;Keyboard: A stream that gives you the set of all keys currently being held down.&#xD;&#xA;Pointers: A powerful stream that combines both mouse and touch inputs into a single list of &quot;pointers.&quot; This lets you build interactions that work seamlessly with both a mouse and a touchscreen.&#xD;&#xA;Activity: Simple streams that let you know if a user is currently active, or if touch input is being used specifically.&#xD;&#xA;Input State: The main, all-in-one stream. This provides a single object containing the complete state of all inputs (mouse, keys, pointers, focus) at any given moment.&#xD;&#xA;Instead of handling many different raw input events, you can connect to these structured streams. This makes it much simpler to build responsive and complex interactions, as all the tricky work of managing input state is done for you.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
